    // divides(c,a) says that c divides a. The \forall in gcd's specification is stated with it,
    // not with %, so that the SMT solver instantiates that quantifier only for divides terms:
    // with % (encoded with div and multiplication by -1) the solver picks an arithmetic trigger,
    // (* -1 c), that matches the terms each instance creates -- a matching loop that never ends
    // (OpenJML issue #997).

